// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Cab File Extraction Via Wusa.EXE From Potentially Suspicious Paths
// Sigma ID: c74c0390-3e20-41fd-a69a-128f0275a5ea
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-05 | Modified: 2023-11-28
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the execution of the "wusa.exe" (Windows Update Standalone Installer) utility to extract
//   ".cab" files using the "/extract" argument from potentially suspicious paths.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20180331144337/https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2018/03/sanny-malware-delivery-method-updated-in-recently-observed-attacks.html
//   - https://www.echotrail.io/insights/search/wusa.exe/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ed4273b30b6bba81f525a9ba136c2bcdb6d8ca95/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wusa_cab_files_extraction_from_susp_paths.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\wusa.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/extract:") and (ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\PerfLogs\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Users\\Public\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":\\Windows\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Appdata\\Local\\Temp\\")
